==Battleground==
*1 [[Croakley]] spawns as the boss.
*3 [[Project A]]s spawn, delay 6.67~8.33 seconds<sup>200f~250f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Tackey]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With the [[Wave Attack|Wave]] [[Talents|Talent]] and maxed [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] is amazing in this stage.

Although maxxed starred alien treasures are not a necessity, it is recommended that you have at least some crystals from [[Cats of the Cosmos]] chapter 2, as with only chapter 1 crystals the stage would be extremely difficult.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Not a lot of Ubers work here, especially ones that are slow-moving. However, most [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] are ones that excel here. Below are more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]]: Can take out the Doge Darks and Tackey fast, basically a no brainer.
*[[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]] & [[D'artanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'artanyan]]: Both insanely good picks for this stage.
*[[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]]: Decent, can hit Tackey from afar, but just don't let him get hit repeatedly, as he has many knockbacks that can disrupt his attack animation.
*[[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars]]: Deals [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] to both [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies, with high DPS that can easily kill off the Doge Darks and pave an easy path to Tackey.

